## Context

The [review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review) shows that matching symptoms and subjects
hid separate parser and form-hint failures. The tenant directory and the running classifier
contradict the subject-only merge rule. Browser-based intake tags also disagree with cause assignments.

## Proposed decision

Replace decision 0001's operational rule with cause-based triage. Keep decision 0001 unchanged
as the record of what was accepted; this proposal still needs the desk's acceptance.
Keep an incoming report separate until its tenant, channel and mechanism are understood.
Use one ticket per demonstrated cause, and count distinct report IDs rather than export rows.

Unknown tenants and contradictory symptoms need investigation. A subject match is a search aid,
not permission to merge. Report intake and merge throughput are separate measurements.

## Consequences

Triage takes more reading. It avoids hiding a second failure under an unrelated queued fix.
Maintain the computed views alongside prose, and review the guidance when data or behavior changes.

